sentences.l:
and he roused all the blasts
of winds of every kind, and with clouds he covered
earth and open-sea together;

And as when the late-summer North Wind carries thistles
over the plain, and close-packed they cling to one another,
so over the open sea the winds carried it here and there;

So then having spoken, the goddess gave the head-veil,
and she herself back into the surging open-sea dived,
like to a shearwater;
